author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Reading any item at any recorded version either returns the reconstructed item or a structured error envelope carrying a code and next steps, never a raw runtime message; A history stream whose first entry carries no document baseline is detected and named as its own condition instead of crashing the read; pm-lty reads successfully at version 1 and at every later recorded version, or returns a named non-crash condition explaining why version 1 has no baseline; Regression coverage includes a stream with no create entry and a stream whose baseline comes from history_compact_baseline; The exit code and envelope shape for a failed point-in-time read conform to the documented error-code contract"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: Detect absent or incomplete history baselines before materialization and return the named history_baseline_unavailable refusal with recovery guidance.
expected_result: "Historical reads return a reconstructed document or a typed actionable error, never an undefined metadata runtime crash."
actual_result: Missing-create and incomplete-baseline negative controls passed alongside complete update-baseline and compacted-baseline compatibility cases. Full repository tests and error-contract checks passed.
